It is not a copy of the SameDayDesk repository, not a second payment stack,
not a job queue or ledger, and not a live settlement engine. The merchant
HTTP adapter does not extract vendor archives at runtime and does not
download GitHub URLs.

Accepted customer input is JSON objects with a `rows` array of
`{field, value, unit}`. Filesystem paths, commands, URLs, and writable
caches are not accepted. `purchaseAuthority` and `paidValueClaim` stay
false. Curated row compares are not live market prices, ROI, or demand.

The merchant repository LICENSE (MIT, SameDayDesk) covers this projection.
